WEBVTT

00:00.680 --> 00:05.480
<i>The author I met through work turned 
out to be a friend from my childhood.</i>

00:06.380 --> 00:08.320
<i>I can't believe it's actually him.</i>

00:08.650 --> 00:11.070
<i>The fact that we met again at my work</i>

00:11.070 --> 00:13.410
<i>must mean that he's been 
working hard all this time.</i>

00:13.620 --> 00:17.730
<i>With this assignment, I don't want to 
do anything half-hearted like back then,</i>

00:17.730 --> 00:19.630
<i>when I failed to return his novel.</i>

00:20.500 --> 00:23.740
<i>But I can't think of a single decent idea.</i>

00:24.010 --> 00:28.910
<i>I need an ad that will make Motoharu glad 
that I was the one working with him.</i>

00:26.000 --> 00:29.460
<b>Swish swish</b>

00:29.710 --> 00:32.660
<i>Huh? My cursor isn't moving.</i>

00:29.710 --> 00:32.670
<b>Draft novel</b>

00:29.720 --> 00:30.550
<b>Swish</b>

00:31.550 --> 00:32.670
Silence

00:33.070 --> 00:34.620
<i>And I was just about to start!</i>

00:34.920 --> 00:37.120
Mima? Can I talk to you for a second?

00:37.810 --> 00:38.730
What are you doing?

00:38.730 --> 00:40.550
My mouse isn't working.

00:40.550 --> 00:41.780
Really?

00:41.780 --> 00:42.530
Let me have a look.

00:42.530 --> 00:43.580
Mints?!

00:43.580 --> 00:45.610
Huh? You want to look at my mints?

02:16.490 --> 02:20.200
<b>#18 
Takayuki and Motoharu</b>

02:16.510 --> 02:17.970
That explains it.

02:18.270 --> 02:20.570
I was wondering what that rattling was...

02:21.560 --> 02:23.280
Maybe you should take a break.

02:23.610 --> 02:25.000
I don't have much time.

02:25.000 --> 02:26.010
I'll be fine.

02:26.010 --> 02:29.120
I get that you're excited to 
be working with a friend, but...

02:29.120 --> 02:29.570
What?

02:29.940 --> 02:33.910
Igarashi Motoharu-sensei 
is Mima-san's friend?

02:33.910 --> 02:36.470
Wait, you know that author?

02:36.470 --> 02:38.040
You don't strike me as a reader.

02:38.040 --> 02:41.030
Yes, because he writes lyrics 
for my friend's band.

02:41.030 --> 02:43.770
Sometimes he's even involved 
in composing their songs!

02:43.770 --> 02:44.610
Huh.

02:44.890 --> 02:48.250
He said that working with the band was great

02:48.250 --> 02:50.700
for letting off steam and 
getting some fresh ideas.

02:51.070 --> 02:53.140
Mima-san, you should 
let off some steam too.

02:53.470 --> 02:55.560
Then I'll go out for a little bit.

02:55.560 --> 02:57.080
Have fun.

02:57.650 --> 02:58.570
<b>AWK</b>

02:57.860 --> 02:58.810
Actually!

02:58.810 --> 03:01.080
Fix your pocket lining that's
sticking out before you go!

03:01.770 --> 03:05.250
<i>What kind of ad should 
we run in the stations?</i>

03:05.250 --> 03:10.070
<i>I hope we can make good use of that limited space 
to connect it to the story somehow...</i>

03:10.760 --> 03:13.190
<i>The story is about an awkward guy</i>

03:13.190 --> 03:15.540
<i>who tries not to repeat the 
same mistakes every day.</i>

03:15.540 --> 03:17.700
<i>So he writes his daily 
blunders into a diary,</i>

03:17.700 --> 03:20.320
<i>but he loses this diary somewhere, 
and that's where the story begins.</i>

03:20.770 --> 03:24.040
<i>A small event eventually 
turns into a big thing.</i>

03:24.410 --> 03:27.940
<i>I think Motoharu would be happy 
if I could make that work.</i>

03:27.680 --> 03:28.310
<b>Fall</b>

03:30.390 --> 03:32.980
<i>This is... oddly relevant.</i>

03:32.980 --> 03:34.650
Excuse me, that's mine.

03:34.960 --> 03:36.400
Thanks for picking it up.

03:36.400 --> 03:38.400
It fell out of my bag...

03:38.870 --> 03:41.060
Moto... Igarashi-san?

03:43.110 --> 03:43.980
Here you go.

03:43.980 --> 03:45.940
Thank you so much.

03:45.940 --> 03:47.140
Cheers.

03:51.470 --> 03:54.350
Somehow, we wandered into the park...

03:54.350 --> 03:59.050
So, um, you're living in Kyoto now, correct?

03:59.050 --> 04:01.360
I'm planning to move here to Tokyo.

04:01.360 --> 04:04.510
I wanted to check out the
 surrounding area before I move.

04:04.510 --> 04:05.940
I see.

04:05.940 --> 04:09.680
Were you out here taking a break from work?

04:09.680 --> 04:10.960
Something like that.

04:11.260 --> 04:13.390
<i>"I wasn't getting anywhere with work..."</i>

04:13.390 --> 04:15.430
<i>is not something I can tell him.</i>

04:18.670 --> 04:20.280
<i>This is awkward.</i>

04:20.280 --> 04:22.690
<i>And it's also too late 
to bring up the past...</i>

04:22.690 --> 04:24.300
Oh, a dog.

04:25.330 --> 04:26.800
I'm really sorry!

04:26.800 --> 04:28.020
I let go of the leash.

04:28.320 --> 04:30.250
We're lucky Sakura-chan's a good dog.

04:30.570 --> 04:31.960
Yeah, for real.

04:32.360 --> 04:35.680
Hayate-san, dogs have way 
more power than hamsters.

04:36.010 --> 04:37.000
I'm sorry.

04:37.000 --> 04:39.640
I shouldn't have even asked to walk her.

04:39.640 --> 04:40.880
I mean, it's no biggie.

04:40.880 --> 04:42.180
Hayate-kun?

04:42.180 --> 04:43.840
Souma-kun and Shun-kun?

04:44.280 --> 04:45.610
Mima-san!

04:46.580 --> 04:47.750
I'm sorry.

04:47.750 --> 04:48.790
She's my dog.

04:49.120 --> 04:50.780
It's no problem at all.

04:50.780 --> 04:51.930
I'm sorry.

04:51.930 --> 04:52.800
This is all my fault.

04:53.100 --> 04:56.960
Shun said he wanted to take her on a walk 
after work, so we all came with him.

04:56.960 --> 04:58.030
My deepest apologies.

04:58.030 --> 04:59.320
This is all because of me.

04:59.320 --> 05:02.180
Hayate-san, you're really 
serious about animals.

05:03.370 --> 05:05.240
So that's why you're all here.

05:03.610 --> 05:04.320
<b>Nod</b>

05:05.730 --> 05:07.900
<i>I wonder if that's someone 
from Mima-san's work...</i>

05:08.240 --> 05:10.230
<i>I feel like I've seen him somewhere.</i>

05:11.300 --> 05:13.350
We're intruding, so let's go over there.

05:13.350 --> 05:14.230
Sounds good.

05:14.230 --> 05:16.030
I'll show you Sakura's tricks.

05:16.030 --> 05:16.590
Cool!

05:16.890 --> 05:19.190
I'm teaching her a new move right now.

05:19.190 --> 05:20.290
A move?

05:20.290 --> 05:21.030
What is it?

05:21.430 --> 05:23.160
Well, Sakura's a genius dog,

05:22.440 --> 05:24.490
<i>Somehow I feel more relaxed...</i>

05:23.160 --> 05:25.680
so she can already shake, sit, 
and stay no problem.

05:25.680 --> 05:26.350
So...

05:26.350 --> 05:27.730
This was unexpected.

05:27.730 --> 05:28.460
What is?

05:28.830 --> 05:31.470
Your friends are all so young.

05:31.470 --> 05:32.170
Yeah.

05:32.550 --> 05:37.010
Until now, I didn't really have 
anything in common with young people.

05:37.400 --> 05:39.330
But once I got to know them,

05:39.330 --> 05:42.980
they reminded me of feelings I had almost 
forgotten and gave me new insights.

05:43.210 --> 05:46.800
So now I think that the presence of 
friends like these is a good thing.

05:47.830 --> 05:49.800
You're right.

05:50.520 --> 05:54.220
In my past, I had a good friend.

05:54.220 --> 05:55.870
Encountering him became the catalyst

05:55.870 --> 05:58.330
for me to realize that there 
is another way of thinking.

05:58.330 --> 06:02.410
"Encounters" really are the 
best catalyst for change.

06:02.410 --> 06:04.030
It's not limited to people, either—

06:04.030 --> 06:07.190
it can be with books, movies, music, or nature.

06:07.190 --> 06:08.890
Even things that feel banal.

06:08.970 --> 06:15.100
<b>Massage</b>

06:09.580 --> 06:12.820
It's always something from 
the outside that comes

06:12.820 --> 06:15.220
and massages out our stiffened world view.

06:15.500 --> 06:19.320
Since your job creates the 
opportunities for these encounters,

06:19.650 --> 06:21.860
I really think it's a wonderful thing.

06:23.240 --> 06:28.110
<i>Ads serve the important role of 
bringing things and people together,</i>

06:28.510 --> 06:31.400
<i>yet so far, I've only been preoccupied 
with pleasing Motoharu.</i>

06:31.400 --> 06:35.830
<i>I hadn't even considered the people who 
should be encountering the product.</i>

06:36.960 --> 06:39.500
You've gotten really quiet.  
Is everything all right?

06:39.500 --> 06:40.670
Oh, it's fine.

06:42.170 --> 06:45.380
I just realized that I had lost sight 
of something really fundamental.

06:45.860 --> 06:47.640
<i>Encounters, huh?</i>

06:48.220 --> 06:51.030
<i>Hayate-kun was a big fan 
of the original works.</i>

06:51.030 --> 06:55.850
<i>It's important to find something that 
doesn't destroy the image held by the fans.</i>

06:56.440 --> 06:59.460
<i>Shun-kun doesn't strike me as a big reader,</i>

06:59.460 --> 07:03.270
<i>which is exactly why the ad needs to shine 
in a way that makes the movie interesting.</i>

07:03.710 --> 07:09.030
<i>Souma-kun will probably pause and 
look if it's creative and playful.</i>

07:10.240 --> 07:11.750
Uh, Shun-kun.

07:12.100 --> 07:14.220
Sakura-chan's poop is really hard.

07:14.220 --> 07:15.160
I hope she's okay.

07:15.160 --> 07:16.860
Oh, yeah. It's like a rock.

07:16.860 --> 07:17.990
That <i>is</i> a rock.

07:20.480 --> 07:23.340
Those kids are kind of funny.

07:23.340 --> 07:25.820
I wonder if they'd be friends with me, too.

07:27.540 --> 07:30.040
They really are funny.

07:32.990 --> 07:34.820
Thanks, Motoharu.

07:34.820 --> 07:36.460
I'm really glad I ran into you today.

07:38.950 --> 07:40.670
Wait, you just called me by my...

07:40.560 --> 07:41.140
<b> Serious</b>

07:40.670 --> 07:42.640
I'll be returning to work now.

07:42.640 --> 07:44.410
There's something I want 
to get done right away.

07:44.620 --> 07:47.550
Guys, I'm leaving now.

07:47.550 --> 07:48.980
See you later!

07:48.980 --> 07:52.280
I'll be in touch with you 
soon, Igarashi-sensei.

07:52.280 --> 07:53.890
Next time, as a friend.

07:53.890 --> 07:54.710
What?

07:55.370 --> 07:56.460
Mima-san!

07:56.820 --> 07:59.440
I mean, Takayuki.

08:01.920 --> 08:04.990
<i>He remembered me.</i>

08:06.090 --> 08:07.800
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

08:08.310 --> 08:09.550
Hey, did you hear?

08:09.550 --> 08:13.350
There's a fun ad up in Shinjuku 
Station for a movie.

08:13.350 --> 08:15.650
A lot of people are posting about it online too.

08:15.650 --> 08:16.510
Show me.

08:16.510 --> 08:18.500
Wait, what?

08:16.510 --> 08:20.100
<b>Nagano
 There's a place at Shinjuku Station 
where you can write your fails.
 I've done this before.</b>

08:16.510 --> 08:20.100
Didn't plug in my earphones
 in on the train and everybody
 heard everything.
FML

08:18.500 --> 08:19.740
Can anyone write on it?

08:20.380 --> 08:21.560
Isn't that the spot?

08:21.560 --> 08:22.820
Let's write one too!

08:23.770 --> 08:26.230
<b>The Lost Diary</b>

08:33.610 --> 08:33.860
<b>Stick</b>

08:37.480 --> 08:40.100
<i>His job really is amazing.</i>

08:37.490 --> 08:41.910
<b>The Lost Diary
 Premieres August 11th
 In this metropolis of Tokyo,
 why not try dropping an 
embarrassing story of how 
you messed up.
 Your story starts right now.</b>

08:44.450 --> 08:46.810
<i>People's failure stories?</i>

08:44.460 --> 08:48.920
<b>I mixed up the meeting time and 
the time I needed to leave my house
 I was SO LATE
 I need to not get wrong things stuck in my head</b>

08:46.810 --> 08:48.910
<i>Is this the ad campaign for the movie?</i>

08:49.430 --> 08:52.810
<i>The advertisement only comes into 
being when people participate.</i>

08:52.810 --> 08:55.020
<i>It's a design that involves the people.</i>

08:56.210 --> 09:00.610
That ad was so fun that I was almost 
late for meeting my friends.

09:00.610 --> 09:03.110
I feel like you'd have a lot to write.

09:03.110 --> 09:03.700
Did you write one?

09:03.700 --> 09:04.470
I did.

09:04.720 --> 09:07.340
Mima was actually in charge of that.

09:07.340 --> 09:08.690
Really?

09:08.980 --> 09:10.280
<i>So that was Mima-san's...</i>

09:11.890 --> 09:16.000
<i>I want to become an adult who 
can do cool work like that, too.</i>

09:14.990 --> 09:15.700
<b>Open</b>

09:16.490 --> 09:18.000
<b>RICE!!</b>

09:17.240 --> 09:18.000
<b>~ Left Uncooked ~</b>

09:18.500 --> 09:19.790
Sorry, bro.

09:19.790 --> 09:21.190
I'll be starting the rice right now.

09:21.190 --> 09:22.810
What?!

09:22.810 --> 09:25.370
I was just so distracted 
thinking about that ad!

09:25.370 --> 09:27.310
Don't make such charming excuses!

09:27.310 --> 09:29.020
I can't get mad at you now!

09:28.750 --> 09:29.960
<b>Growl</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>Coming up next</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>New Member</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
